cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Solar PV Dynamic Characterization, Global MPPT & Boost Stage Solver"
message: "If you use this photovoltaic model, MPPT benchmark suite, or power-stage solver in academic, research, or engineering work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Haris
    family-names: Zafar
    alias: hariszafar740-lang
repository-code: "https://github.com/hariszafar740-lang/solar-pv-mppt-dynamic-solver"
url: "https://hariszafar740-lang.github.io/solar-pv-mppt-dynamic-solver/"
abstract: >-
  Multi-physics Python solver and interactive workbench for single-diode solar
  photovoltaic modules (De Soto / CEC formulation cross-validated against NREL
  SAM and pvlib Lambert-W), Schottky bypass-diode partial-shading strings,
  Global MPPT (PSO and Hybrid Global-Scan + Adaptive INC), CENELEC EN 50530
  dynamic irradiance ramps with coupled electro-thermal cell ODE and Sera
  dP-P&O, and a state-space averaged DC-DC boost converter with cascaded
  average-current-mode PI control and component loss maps.
keywords:
  - photovoltaics
  - solar-energy
  - single-diode-model
  - partial-shading
  - global-mppt
  - en-50530
  - boost-converter
  - power-electronics
  - pvlib
  - python
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
